  "prompt_text": "The figure outlines a closed-loop platform for AI-guided chemical discovery that links automated experiments, machine-learning models, planning, and robotic synthesis. At the top left, compounds are tested and automatically characterized, producing pass/fail or assay-style outcomes shown as heatmap-like matrices. These experimental results are archived and fed back to update a reward model.\n\nOn the right, surrogate models based on an encoder–decoder architecture with attention appear to translate molecular representations into predicted outputs, which are then used to estimate a reward function. External knowledge sources such as databases, journals, patents, and simulations also feed into the modelling and natural language processing steps, indicating that both experimental and literature-derived information are used.\n\nThe lower right panel shows planning or optimization over a network of candidate molecules, where a promising starting structure branches into related analogs and selected paths are highlighted, suggesting guided exploration of chemical space toward higher-value compounds. The lower left panel depicts automated synthesis with a robotic arm dispensing into vials, closing the loop by making the predicted best candidates. Overall, the image conveys an integrated self-improving workflow in which models propose molecules, robots make and test them, and new data continuously refine future decisions.",
